      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1812, a woolen factory opened in what became Factory Village, spurred by the town’s abundant sheep farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://colebrooknh.org/history/41-2/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first street lamp in Colebrook lit up in 1876, illuminating the town’s growing streets for the first time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://colebrooknh.org/history/historical-information/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad in 1887 shifted Colebrook’s economy from stagecoach routes to rail‑connected manufacturing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
